---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const habits = [
  'Self-awareness', 'Emotional responsibility', 'Truthful speech', 'Compassion',
  'Nonviolence', 'Reverence for life', 'Disciplined imagination',
  'Willingness to heal inherited pain', 'Commitment to serve more than the ego',
];
const questions = [
  'Does it reduce suffering?', 'Does it increase dignity?', 'Does it strengthen peace?',
  'Does it deepen truth and transparency?', 'Does it serve the many, not just the few?',
  'Does it protect nature?', 'Does it build trust, healing and belonging?',
  'Does it help future generations?', 'Does it align with unity rather than separation?',
  'Would we be proud to let children inherit it?',
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Inner Blueprint"
  description="Explore the Inner Blueprint: reflective habits and questions that connect inner responsibility with practical system design."
  canonical="/blueprint/inner-blueprint/"
>
  <article class="content-page">
    <header class="page-hero shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inner responsibility and outer design</p>
      <h1>The Inner Blueprint</h1>
      <p class="lede">The Inner Blueprint explores the relationship between consciousness, responsibility and the systems people create. It is a reflective foundation, not a prescribed belief system.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="shell content-flow">
      <section>
        <h2>Habits that support the work</h2>
        <p>The repository foundation identifies the following habits as useful starting points:</p>
        <ul>{habits.map((habit) => <li>{habit}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Questions for alignment</h2>
        <p>Before treating a system as aligned with New Earth, the existing New Earth Test asks:</p>
        <ol>{questions.map((question) => <li>{question}</li>)}</ol>
        <p>These questions are prompts for scrutiny and conversation. They do not certify a project or replace evidence, specialist review or accountable decision-making.</p>
      </section>
      <nav class="page-actions" aria-label="Continue exploring">
        <a class="button" href="/blueprint/transition-path/">Explore the Transition Path</a>
        <a class="button" href="/blueprint/pillars/">Explore the 12 Pillars</a>
        <a class="button" href="/blueprint/">Back to the Blueprint</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
